</mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig position="float" id="F1"><label>Fig 1.</label><caption><title>Awake deep brain stimulation (DBS) surgical workflow.</title><p id="P36">(A) Preoperative planning integrates indirect targeting (ACPC coordinates), deformed atlases, and structural and diffusion imaging (FGATIR, tractography) to define surgical targets and trajectories. (B) Microelectrode recordings (MER) involves inserting high-impedance electrodes into target structures to record single-cell activity and local field potentials. (C) Macrostimulation testing uses the ring electrode to assess therapeutic efficacy and side effect thresholds to confirm or reposition the lead. (D) In suboptimal cases, additional tracks can be tested. These moves may be closer to the target, correcting for stereotactic error, or farther/equidistant moves that would typically not be made by imaging alone.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="nihpp-2025.09.25.25336654v1-f0001" position="float"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F2"><label>Fig 2.</label><caption><title>Features of microelectrode recordings (MER) used for optimal deep brain stimulation (DBS) lead placement.</title><p id="P37">MER identifies white to gray matter transitions based on single-unit firing and background (e.g. quiet white matter into highly active subthalamic nucleus). Characteristic firing patterns can also be distinguished between regions, such as bursting or pausing cells in the external globus pallidus (GPe), and border and irregular firing cells in the internal globus pallidus (GPi). Neurons in the ventral intermediate nucleus of the thalamus (VIM) may be tuned to passive movement (kinesthetic cells) or pathologic tremor as seen on electromyography (EMG).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="nihpp-2025.09.25.25336654v1-f0002" position="float"/></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1.</label><caption><p id="P38">Final lead placement and physiologic deviation in VIM deep brain stimulation (DBS) cases.</p></caption><table frame="box" rules="cols"><colgroup span="1"><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/></colgroup><thead><tr style="border-bottom: solid 1px"><th align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Lead Side</th><th align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Initial Track(s)</th><th align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Final Track</th><th align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Implant Depth (mm)</th><th align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Direction</th><th align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Distance (mm)</th><th align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Angle (&#x000b0;)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">R</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center; posterior</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">posterior</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Toward</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.4</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">250</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">L</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center; medial</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">medial</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;2</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Away</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.0</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">90</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">L</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">posterior</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;0.5</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Away</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.1</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">180</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">R</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">posterior</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;1</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Away</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.2</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">190</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">L</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center; posterior</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">posterior</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Away</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.0</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">160</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">L</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center; medial</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">medial</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Away</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.0</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">90</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">L</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">medial</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;1</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Toward</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.0</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">R</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">anterior</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;1</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Away</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.8</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">R</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center; posterior</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">posterior</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Away</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.8</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">225</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">L</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center; posterior</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">medial</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;1</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Away</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.5</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">90</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">L</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">medial</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02212;1</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Away</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.7</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">80</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">L</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center; medial; anterior</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">medial</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Same</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.0</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">90</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">R</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">anterior</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Away</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.4</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">R</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center; anterior</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">anterior</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.5</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Away</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.7</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">R</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">anterior</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Away</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.7</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">L</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center; posterior</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">posterior</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Away</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.3</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">180</td></tr><tr><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">L</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">center; posterior</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">posterior</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0</td><td align="left" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Same</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.0</td><td align="right" valign="middle" rowspan="1" colspan="1">180</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="TFN1"><p id="P39">Deviations in final DBS lead placement relative to the imaging-defined center track. These deviations may reflect results from microelectrode recording (MER), macrostimulation testing, or both. &#x0201c;Toward&#x0201d; indicates movement closer to the preoperative target; &#x0201c;Away&#x0201d; indicates deviation based on physiologic data; &#x0201c;Same&#x0201d; indicates a move across the planned target resulting in the same distance.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T2"><label>Table 2.</label><caption><p id="P40">Definitions of microelectrode recording (MER) strategies in DBS surgery.</p></caption><table frame="box" rules="all"><colgroup span="1"><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">MER Strategy</th><th align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Definition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Exploratory</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">A mapping strategy that uses multiple (3&#x02013;5) simultaneous initial parallel tracts to characterize the target region volumetrically. Employed when target anatomy is ambiguous or distorted, allowing for selection of the trajectory with the most robust physiologic signature.</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Confirmatory</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">A physiologically guided approach used to verify the presence of expected neural activity along the planned trajectory. Typically involves 1&#x02013;2 electrodes and informs minor adjustments, especially in depth, to optimize lead placement based on intraoperative signals. Addition of subsequent tracts is indicated by pattern of neural activity, behavioral testing, and response to stimulation.</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Nominal</td><td align="left" valign="top" rowspan="1" colspan="1">A minimal recording approach often performed for documentation or billing, without intent to influence surgical decisions. Provides limited physiologic data and is not used to guide final lead placement.</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></floats-group></article>